      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T18:00:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are your thoughts on making some of this behavior (particularly the tone-mapping, which seems fairly chrome-specific?) pluggable? Can we let the caller supply a std::function for clut construction, or soemthing like that, and then have a large chunk of the math be supplied by chrome (vs. the mechanical aspects of the table building, that could live here)?",
      "revId": "25af8b8f47411a2b7d2d80dc8ee39dbb54834ed6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e23e2b35_dde7ecb4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-29T22:53:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That seems like quite a reasonable way for things to go.\n\nIf we do expose an API for this, the API will ultimately end up being \"pass an skcms_ICCProfile\" (or maybe an skcms_ICCProfile where all the data is represented as floats).\n\nThis is because, while I happen to just be using a 17x17x17 LUT here, there are lots of people trying to do clever-er things, which would take advantage of the full A/B/M curves and matrix, and might be much more (space) efficient. Just having some simple function callback for clut construction won\u0027t be enough.\n\nI think that the long-term way that we will end up doing this will be to\n- Move the functionality of SkWriteICCProfile into an skcms method that takes an skcms_ICCProfile\n- Maybe add some \"nice-ities\" to skcms_ICCProfile (like representing LUTs and curvs as floats instead of fixed-point, and just specify an argument saying \"this will serialize to 8 bit\")\n- Delete SkWriteICCProfile\nAt that point, skia will neither decide the tone mapping (that will be Chrome), nor write the ICC profile (that will be skcms).\n\nBut that\u0027s a bit of a big lift, and I worry that we\u0027ll lose momentum on this (and potentially just never end up doing it) if we don\u0027t make this short-term compromise (which in this case would be growing the skia code, which ultimately I think will shrink back to nonexistence as its pushed out to skcms and Chrome).",
      "parentUuid": "5a570770_7d1199b8",
      "revId": "25af8b8f47411a2b7d2d80dc8ee39dbb54834ed6",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
